roposed site is southwest of Gaza and another northeast of Beersheba, and neither is certain.","place",1],["madmannah","Madmannah","Man living at the time of Divided Monarchy","1 Chronicles names him once, and he is a man from the divided-kingdom years.","person",1]],"v":[6233,10355]},"H4028":{"l":"מִגְדַּל־גָּד","x":"Migdal-Gâd","d":"Migdal-Gad, a place in Palestine","p":"migdal-gawd'","t":"migdal-gad","g":"Migdal","fb":[["migdal-gad","Migdal-gad","","In the lowland district of Judah, the Shephelah. The name means \"tower of Gad,\" and it is generally placed at el-Mejdel near Ashkelon, which still keeps the word migdal.","place",1]],"v":[6239,6239]},"H4081":{"l":"מִדִּין","x":"Middîyn","d":null,"p":"mid-deen'","t":"middin","g":"Middin","fb":[["middin","Middin","","\"Measures.\" One of the six towns in the wilderness west of the Dead Sea, listed with En-gedi.","place",1]],"v":[6263]},"H4027":{"l":"מִגְדַּל־אֵל","x":"Migdal-ʼÊl","d":"Migdal-El, a place in Palestine","p":"mig-dal-ale'","t":"migdal-el","g":"Migdal","fb":[["migdal-el","Migdal-el","","\"Tower of God,\" a fortified town of Naphtali. Some scholars have tied it to Magdala, Mary Magdalene's town, but the link is not certain.","place",1]],"v":[6359,6359]},"H4051":{"l":"מִגְרוֹן","x":"Migrôwn","d":"Migron, a place in Palestine","p":"mig-rone'","t":"migron","g":"Migron","fb":[["migron","Migron","","Saul camped under a pomegranate tree at Migron, near Gibeah, with about six hundred men, just before Jonathan's raid on the Philistines at Michmash. Isaiah has an invading army pass a Migron near Aiath, apparently a different spot of the same name.","place",2]],"v":[7510,17877]},"H4063":{"l":"מֶדֶו","x":"medev","d":"properly, extent, i.e. measure; by implication, a dress (as measured)","p":"meh'-dev","t":"medev","g":"robes","fb":[],"v":[8244,10911]},"H4050":{"l":"מְגֵרָה","x":"mᵉgêrâh","d":"a saw","p":"meg-ay-raw'","t":"megerah","g":"saw","fb":[],"v":[8317,8943,10929,10929]},"H4037":{"l":"מַגְזֵרָה","x":"magzêrâh","d